meta {
  name: refresh token (rest-auth alias)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/token/refresh/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // Refresh token from the login response. Required.
    "refresh": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  dj-rest-auth's refresh endpoint. Functionally the same as
  **get access token** (`/get-access-token/`) -- it also reads the refresh token
  from the `refresh` cookie when one is set, which this project does not use
  (`JWT_AUTH_HTTPONLY = False`, so the frontend holds the tokens).

  Pick one and stay with it; `/get-access-token/` is the one the rest of this
  collection uses.

  ## API example response
  {
    "access": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
  }
}
